WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.940
What? Ren's staying over? Why?

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.440
I can go pick him up.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.730
<i>You're so overprotective.</i>

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.840
<i>What are you so worried about?</i>

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.200
But he didn't say anything earlier.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:19.300
Haru, it upsets him when 
you treat him like a little kid.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.700
<i>What? Ren's mad?</i>

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.430
<i>Are you stupid?</i>

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.490
<i>If you want to keep Ren around forever, 
this is having the opposite effect.</i>

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.900
I hope you don't regret it.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.300
What? Is Ren staying out overnight?

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.070
Ren will probably feel more 
at ease with Natsuo.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:48.950
He must be tired of playing 
the difficult younger brother.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.570
We're talking about Ren, right?

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.450
Aki, don't you think the 
same thing sometimes?

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.950
Yeah, but it's dangerous to leave him 
alone with our worthless brother.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.950
I can hear everything you're saying!

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.110
Hey. Looks like you slept well.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.640
When did you come back?

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.540
About thirty minutes ago.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.030
The lights were off, so I thought 
you got scared and went home.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.980
But I can understand why your first 
step toward becoming an adult

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.660
would be to do something 
you can't tell Haru about.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.790
He can be weirdly serious about things.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.080
It seems like you don't care about anything.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.370
What? If you don't want me, 
I can call a girl.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.800
Women are too much trouble.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.240
You're too young to be so insightful.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.810
I can tell just by watching 
Haru and the twins.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.940
So you want a man to be your first?

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.360
Does Haru not do anything for you?

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.470
He said he wouldn't have sex with 
me because I'm an ignorant child.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:44.590
Huh... I'm not interested in men or kids,

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.620
but I might be able to 
handle it if it's with you.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.830
Really? That's convenient.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.160
You're quite the man, aren't you?

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.550
Wait, let me see this...

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.840
<i>Oh, my.</i>

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.310
<i>He won't have sex with him?</i>

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.610
<i>How can that idiot say that</i>

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:07.700
<i>after leaving these marks on him?</i>

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:08.350
Natsuo?

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.120
Take off your clothes.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:10.960
Here?

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.810
Don't be such a girl.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.850
Want me to carry you to bed?

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.030
Fine. Forget it.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.360
<i>I didn't think it would bother me.</i>

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.390
<i>He smells different from Haru.</i>

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.880
<i>The way he touches me is different. 
The way he acts is different.</i>

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.830
<i>Everything is different.</i>

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:31.760
And?

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:39.130
How long are you going 
to keep playing with fire?

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.340
Huh? Haru, how'd you get in?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.780
We traded keys the other day, remember?

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.510
Our homes are open to each other.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.010
I had a bad feeling, 
so I came to pick you up.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:50.890
What's going on, Ren?

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.870
What were you going to do with Natsuo?

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:59.180
You said I was an ignorant child,

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:01.900
so I just thought I'd try some things out.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:05.300
So you decided to get some 
experience with a man you know?

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.160
This is why I said you were stupid!

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.620
But you won't do anything!

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.550
I'm tired of being treated like a kid!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:11.940
Hey...

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.910
This kind of behavior is what makes you a child.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.160
Hey, hang on.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.420
Now that your guardian's here, 
it can't be helped.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.630
Ren, you should go home.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:21.240
No.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.680
What good does arguing do?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.160
Your brother's over there glaring at you.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.180
No, do whatever you want.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:32.530
If you really think that'll make you an adult,

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.060
then why don't you try doing it with Natsuo?

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.640
But if you do...

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:43.050
Ren, don't ever come back.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.070
Ren?

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:51.460
I'm going home.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.710
Well, it's for the best.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.650
Haru was actually mad this time.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:58.190
I'll take you home. Give me a minute.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.040
It's fine.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.920
I'm going to walk for a bit.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.000
I'll take a taxi the rest of the way.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.040
Huh? Hey, Ren...

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.090
Haru...

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.270
Get in.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.620
You're going home, right?

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:34.280
They really are a pain in the ass.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:46.250
<i>I never thought I'd have a home to return to,</i>

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.540
<i>even after I started living with Haru.</i>

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:50.220
<i>But...</i>

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:55.000
Don't ever come back.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:55.430
Don't ever come back.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.940
Ren, are you asleep?

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:03.010
Ren?

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.940
<i>Does that mean I can't be with Haru anymore?</i>

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:15.580
Come on.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:19.840
Take a bath and go to bed.

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:20.540
Haru...

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:23.300
In your own room.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.070
Haru!

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:27.790
I don't want to sleep in the same room as a kid

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.800
who indiscriminately sleeps around!

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.840
What was that?

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.990
It's not as though I'd do it with anyone.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:36.160
Were you doing it to spite me, then?

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.580
Why else would it be Natsuo, of all people?

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.870
Don't drag him into your curiosity!

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.180
Then you should've done it.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.550
Like I'd ever do it with a brat like you!

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.500
Stay away from Natsuo!

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:08.680
Ren?

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.240
Re—

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:19.280
<i>Oh, right... Yesterday, I...</i>

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.680
<i>I shouldn't have done that!</i>

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:25.060
<i>But what's wrong with Ren?</i>

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.190
<i>When I told him to stay away from Natsuo,</i>

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.820
<i>why did he look like he was going to cry?</i>

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:32.940
<i>Does that mean...</i>

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.100
Kiyoka-san, is something wrong?

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:46.230
Is something wrong? Do you not think 
there's something wrong with that?

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:46.960
Oh...

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.640
It is unusual.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:57.880
He normally never accepts 
gifts from customers.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:02.150
Oh, God... Those aren't 
homemade sweets, are they?

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:07.270
What is he going to tell your 
youngest brother if he finds them?

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.730
It's probably partially on purpose.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.990
Oh? Is he fighting with your
youngest brother again?

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.490
You seem to be enjoying this, Kiyoka-san.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.490
I love other people's drama!

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.500
Aki, don't eat on my bed.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.550
What? You want some?

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.510
They're limited-availability 
convenience store sweets.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.780
No. What's wrong with you?

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.520
You should eat in your own room.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.960
No way. I don't drink or eat in my room.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.720
It's a hassle to clean up.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:45.520
You...

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.770
More importantly, Ren.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.630
Try not to upset our brother 
too much right now.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.970
He's already not feeling well.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:59.090
Is that because the anniversary of 
his parents' death is coming up?

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:02.950
Yeah. I guess it's like an 
aftereffect of the accident.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.940
It's probably something psychological.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.540
Wasn't he like that last year?

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.540
I don't know.

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:12.210
Last year, I was sent to summer camp,

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.900
so I wasn't with Haru.

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:18.330
Oh, really? So he avoided it.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:20.550
But Haru didn't say anything.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:25.060
Why didn't he talk to the doctor 
if he wasn't feeling well?

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:27.390
Why?

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.740
Because he probably doesn't realize 
it himself. He has no self-awareness.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.320
Anyway, he'll probably reach 
his limit in about a week.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:35.980
Should we leave him alone until then?

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:40.360
Well, our last hope—you—upset him again.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.010
Honestly, what did you do this time?

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:43.830
I didn't do anything.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.940
He stopped me before I could.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:51.550
Either way, all I ever do is upset Haru.

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:54.640
What?

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.890
Ren, listen...

00:10:56.890 --> 00:11:01.640
People think our brother is 
mild-mannered and affable.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:05.460
He rarely ever yells at us, either.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:07.350
But when it comes to you...

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.860
I'm not doing it to upset him.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.840
Well, who cares?

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:20.820
Just imagine he only gets mad 
at you because he really cares.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:25.300
Haru gets mad at me 
because I'm a naïve child.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:28.890
Because I caused trouble 
for Natsuo this time.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:34.910
He probably made a move on you.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:37.340
He's always been a pain in the ass.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:38.840
Aki...

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:39.950
Later.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.360
Aki!

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.990
Iku, you can have this.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:58.230
Isn't this...

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:01.290
the gift you got from a 
customer this afternoon?

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.460
Hey, they're cookies.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:08.000
You don't usually accept gifts, though.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.830
It was more work to say no.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.840
Is the summer heat getting to you?

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:15.750
Haru-san, you've been 
down the past few days.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.390
Maybe.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:19.910
It's been hot lately.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:23.680
If you're feeling under the weather, 
why don't you take another break from work?

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:26.820
It's not that bad.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:30.310
But we should hire some employees soon.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.050
Once summer vacation ends,

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:35.460
your brothers won't be able to help 
around the café all the time.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.890
The store won't be so crowded 
once summer vacation ends.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.440
If we're really short-staffed,

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:44.860
I'll have Kiyo send some of 
her employees. Don't worry.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:46.990
We'd do anything for you, Haru-chan!

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.570
For you, it's free!

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.250
Call us anytime!

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.960
What? From the place on Second Street?!

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.840
Huh? Ren, are you alone?

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:18.080
Aki's at work. Shima's at 
the bookstore by the station.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:21.530
He e-mailed to say he'd be home by dinner.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:25.520
If Aki's not home, we can have 
something light for dinner.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:28.400
Ren, is there anything you want to eat?

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.950
I'll eat anything.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.660
It's easier for me if you have a request.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:34.740
Fine, then.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.420
You don't usually have one. What is it?

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:43.920
I want to start sleeping 
in your room again. Can I?

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:47.910
No.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:48.430
Why not?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:52.390
Don't you get it? I'm mad at you.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:56.310
I never thought you'd 
do something so stupid.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:58.710
I'm sorry I got Natsuo involved.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:01.370
I'll stay away from him in the future.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:05.070
That's not what I meant, Ren.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.450
You don't know what the 
rest of the world considers

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.590
what you were trying to 
do with Natsuo, do you?

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:16.080
You were treating me 
like an ignorant child,

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.170
so I just thought I would get 
experience somewhere else.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.670
Even though you have me?

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.780
You said you didn't want to do it with me.

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:28.470
It's no use. There's no way you'll understand.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.000
I don't get what you're trying to say.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.720
Okay, what if I put it this way?

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.520
I don't want to be in the same room with you

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.510
because you said you loved me but 
then tried to do it with someone else!

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.270
I'm home.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.370
Brother?

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:37.870
Oh, Shima.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:42.600
Sorry, but could you take 
care of dinner tonight?

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.820
Sure, I guess.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:49.200
<i>I need to apologize to Ren.</i>

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:54.890
<i>But it's not my fault in the first place.</i>

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:59.660
<i>I know there's no point 
in lecturing Ren like this...</i>

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:02.900
Ren, are you in there?

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:05.750
Sorry. I went too far earlier.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.210
Ren? Ren?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.330
Ren, earlier—

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:13.160
It's fine.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.310
You don't have to apologize.

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:18.970
It's my fault.

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:22.690
I was wrong about everything.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.730
<i>Really?</i>

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.300
Ren, what's wrong?

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.400
Juuzen.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.970
Is your brain still on summer vacation?

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.310
It's already lunchtime. You should eat.

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.670
I'm not hungry.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:46.400
How can you say that when your 
brother made your lunch for you?

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.960
Trade me yours for my 
convenience store rice balls.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:49.820
Sure.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.320
What? Seriously?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.820
It's too much for me, 
but it's just enough for you.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.000
Are you not hungry because 
the heat is getting to you?

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:04.090
Don't tell me you're still backed up.

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:05.330
Maybe that's what it is.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.560
The summer heat.

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:10.590
It's already September, but it's still hot.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:11.920
Oh, that?

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:15.340
Well, Japan's summers are always like this.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:20.100
But didn't you go cool off in 
Canada over summer break?

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.850
You ignored all my e-mails and calls.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.780
I didn't go back to Canada. 
I dropped my phone in water.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.800
The one I have now is a new one.

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:29.720
Huh?

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:33.360
I worked over the summer
so I could buy a new phone.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.180
You worked?

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:38.860
I cleaned an apartment packed full of trash.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:41.210
I even found the body of a dog in the back.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:44.250
Are you okay?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:47.370
Please don't talk about 
that while I'm eating!

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:50.380
What about you, Juuzen? 
Did you go back home?

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:54.880
Nah. I spent half the break in 
the dorm and half in Osaka.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.860
I thought your family left Osaka.

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:01.380
My sister works as a cabaret girl in Osaka.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.870
I crashed with her.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:04.890
Your sister?

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:07.720
Huh? I didn't tell you?

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:10.400
I have an older brother and sister.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.150
I didn't know.

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:17.200
Well, my sister, who's the oldest, 
left home when she was eighteen.

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:20.130
My brother died when I was in grade school,

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.160
so I don't talk about him much.

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:23.530
He died?

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:24.660
In a boring old accident.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:30.670
My mom still cries when she hears his name,

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.620
so we don't talk about him.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.260
But still...

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:40.310
Trying not to remember only 
makes things more painful.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:00.370
Haru-chan?

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:02.900
Haru-chan.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.160
Haru-chan.

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.540
Haru-chan!

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:10.540
Mom?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.310
We came to pick you up.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:14.160
I'm glad you made it.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:16.050
Haru, you look well.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.280
Dad, you came, too?

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:21.210
Aki's been in a bad mood 
while you were gone.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:23.050
He made me come meet you.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.860
Your brothers wanted to come,

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:29.310
but they grudgingly left this morning 
since they had club practice.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.060
Really?

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:33.060
Anyway, Haru-chan, how was Ren-kun?

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:37.070
What? Mom, how do you know about Ren?

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:41.310
There are no secrets between 
me and Haruko-chan.

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:42.690
Huh? What does that mean?

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:45.390
It's nice to have more family, isn't it?

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:48.080
Yeah, yeah. We can continue 
this discussion in the car.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:55.710
Isn't Ren-kun a good boy?

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:59.030
I'd been wondering about him since

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:02.270
Haruko-chan told me there was 
an unusual boy at the orphanage.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:07.190
She said Lepton and Quark 
seemed to like him quite a bit.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:10.230
Those two grew up with you, remember?

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:13.850
So I knew you had to meet him.

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:16.310
Why?

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:20.370
Well, you're lonely, aren't you, Haru?

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:21.610
So we thought...

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:22.740
Dad, watch out!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:23.680
In front of you!

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:31.370
<i>It's all sticky. What is this?</i>

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:44.060
Dad? Mom?

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.710
Hey, kid! Are you okay?

00:20:57.710 --> 00:20:58.940
We're gonna help you right now!

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:02.820
One seriously wounded 
passenger in the back seat!

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.700
The two in front are...

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:20.610
Well, you're lonely, aren't you, Haru?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:25.630
<i>I am, Dad. But so what?</i>

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:27.150
So we thought...

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:28.060
<i>Thought what?</i>

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.090
<i>What was it?</i>

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.360
<i>I have that dream all the time,</i>

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:46.400
<i>but I can never remember 
what Dad said next.</i>

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:40.340
Next Time
